      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Tetranuclear Dy SMM with two slow magnetic relaxation processes under zero dc field, attributed to two Dy(III) coordination geometries (C4v and C2v) and chloride coordination. Room-temperature χmT = 55.06 cm3 K mol−1 (100 Oe). χmT decreases to 49.87 cm3 K mol−1 at 16 K, rises to 51.88 cm3 K mol−1 at 4 K, then drops to 42.99 cm3 K mol−1 at 1.8 K. Magnetization at 1.8 K reaches 23.75 μB (0–70 kOe). Frequency-dependent ac signals below ~20 K under zero field; Arrhenius fit gives Ueff = 55.71 K and τ0 = 7.54 × 10−6 s. Cole–Cole plots (1.8–10 K) are unsymmetric below 7.5 K and fit two modified Debye functions (α 0.33–0.51).",
        "measurements": [
